  "details": "<p>The basilica is located at the third mile of the Via Latina. It dates to the fifth century and the reign of Pope Leo I. The basilica was built on the site of a suburban villa that belonged to one\u00a0<span>Amnia Demetrias, a convert to Christianity. Evidence of the villa's ownership was uncovered during excavations in 1858.</span></p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "The now-ruined basilica of Santo Stefano in Via Latina was a fifth-century CE early Christian basilica. It is now located within the confines of the archaeological park of the Via Latina tombs.",
